WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.030 --> 00:00:05.050
Yippee-ki-yay movie lovers, it's Jan here
and today I'm answering your Avengers: Infinity

00:00:05.050 --> 00:00:09.160
War questions, plus revealing some more details
from the trailer you might have missed.

00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:13.639
A brand new round of my Marvel giveaway is
also running here and to enter, you just need

00:00:13.639 --> 00:00:18.230
to be a subscriber and comment about the movie
or leave a request for future Infinity War

00:00:18.230 --> 00:00:19.230
videos.

00:00:19.230 --> 00:00:22.200
Plus, I'll announce the winner from my trailer
breakdown later in this video.

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:27.380
Of course, speculation and possible spoilers
ahead for Infinity War and the MCU.

00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:31.400
Let's kick things off with Iron Man and Clemence
who asks "Do you think the rumours of Iron

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:33.340
man using the Bleeding Edge armour are true?"

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:37.739
Well, yes, I do think the new armour we're
seeing hints of in the promos is very likely

00:00:37.739 --> 00:00:40.969
the MCU's take on Iron Man's bleeding edge
armour.

00:00:40.969 --> 00:00:45.129
In the Super Bowl spot, you could see the
new armor forming itself around Tony Stark

00:00:45.129 --> 00:00:49.210
and I suspect it's coming from a new arc reactor
that Tony has designed.

00:00:49.210 --> 00:00:53.710
The official Infinity War prelude comic shows
Tony playing around with a new blue reactor

00:00:53.710 --> 00:00:57.969
in the Avengers Compound, as he prepares for
"the end of all things".

00:00:57.969 --> 00:01:02.600
Iron Man's new blue reactor is a kind of easter
egg to the comic book bleeding edge armour

00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:05.280
that first appeared in The Invincible Iron
Man.

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:09.990
In that comic book storyline, Iron Man's armour
flowed out of the arc reactor wrapping itself

00:01:09.990 --> 00:01:11.689
around Tony Stark.

00:01:11.689 --> 00:01:16.890
In the movie, the new armour will also probably
be a form of nano-technology, like Black Panther's

00:01:16.890 --> 00:01:21.119
suit, although I think this is going to be
something Tony develops by himself and not

00:01:21.119 --> 00:01:22.740
Wakandan tech.

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:27.180
As Lucifer points out, the way the thrusters
on Iron Man's feet morph into a single booster

00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:32.560
may indicate nano tech at work which Tony
can command to form a variety of structures.

00:01:32.560 --> 00:01:36.970
By the way, we haven't seen them in the trailers
yet, but the EW cover for Iron Man shows arm

00:01:36.970 --> 00:01:40.570
wings or boosters which I think we'll also
see him use for additional control when he's

00:01:40.570 --> 00:01:41.880
moving in space.

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:46.479
Next up, a lot of you want to know more about
the Black Order who we got to see a proper

00:01:46.479 --> 00:01:48.670
team shot of in the new trailer.

00:01:48.670 --> 00:01:53.369
In a change from the comics, in the MCU each
member of the Black Order is one of Thanos's

00:01:53.369 --> 00:01:55.820
children, like Nebula and Gamora.

00:01:55.820 --> 00:02:00.969
From left to right in this shot, we have Proxima
Midnight, Ebony Maw, Corvus Glaive and Cull

00:02:00.969 --> 00:02:07.179
Obsidian, whose comic-book name was actually
Black Dwarf.

00:02:07.179 --> 00:02:12.590
The Order were introduced as a team in the
Infinity comic book storyline where they were

00:02:12.590 --> 00:02:15.650
sent to Earth by Thanos to retrieve the Infinity
Gems.

00:02:15.650 --> 00:02:20.040
And it's now been confirmed that, in the Infinity
War movie, the Black Order come down to Earth

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:25.060
on a Q-ship, which is that circular alien
ship seen hovering over New York.

00:02:25.060 --> 00:02:29.230
Indeed, in the first trailer, we already saw
Corvus Glaive attacking Vision for the Mind

00:02:29.230 --> 00:02:30.780
Stone with his blade.

00:02:30.780 --> 00:02:35.170
The weapon which Corvus Glaive wields in the
comics can cut through virtually anything

00:02:35.170 --> 00:02:39.900
or anyone, which is why it's so terrifying
to see it used on Vision.

00:02:39.900 --> 00:02:43.790
This scene likely takes place before Vision
is taken to Wakanda, so I think Vision is

00:02:43.790 --> 00:02:48.140
likely saved at this point, although the way
Scarlet Witch looks at him later in Wakanda

00:02:48.140 --> 00:02:51.140
makes me doubt he'll survive the film.

00:02:51.140 --> 00:02:54.870
Back to the group shot of the Black Order
with Loki, some of you are wondering whether

00:02:54.870 --> 00:02:57.620
Loki has switched sides again back to Thanos.

00:02:57.620 --> 00:03:01.739
Judging by the way Proxima Midnight is pointing
her spear at the God of Mischief, I think

00:03:01.739 --> 00:03:05.810
he's actually being summoned to Thanos to
answer for his failure in the first Avengers

00:03:05.810 --> 00:03:10.140
movie, when he lost the Mind Stone that Thanos
gave him to help his takeover of Earth.

00:03:10.140 --> 00:03:14.780
Now, we know that Loki has changed since then,
and although he's still got an eye for trouble,

00:03:14.780 --> 00:03:17.530
I don't think he's going to switch sides again.

00:03:17.530 --> 00:03:21.920
Loki may have already saved Bruce Banner by
using the Tesseract which he stole from Asgard

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:25.709
to portal him back to Earth to warn the other
Avengers about Thanos.

00:03:25.709 --> 00:03:30.190
And Loki may even try to bargain with Thanos
offering up the Tesseract in exchange perhaps

00:03:30.190 --> 00:03:32.659
for saving his brother, Thor's life.

00:03:32.659 --> 00:03:37.220
Sadly though, I do think Loki's days are probably
numbered and Thanos will execute him after

00:03:37.220 --> 00:03:38.900
he gives up the Space Stone.

00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:41.209
Hopefully it will be a heroic death though.

00:03:41.209 --> 00:03:45.299
There's also another interesting detail in
this shot with some fans pointing out that

00:03:45.299 --> 00:03:48.739
there's a sword lying on the ground which
looks like it could be the Bifrost Sword that

00:03:48.739 --> 00:03:52.890
Heimdall normally wields, though it's hard
to be sure from this image if the hilt is

00:03:52.890 --> 00:03:54.280
exactly the same.

00:03:54.280 --> 00:03:59.019
But if it is, then that's pretty bad news
for Heimdall as I suspect it means Thanos

00:03:59.019 --> 00:04:03.200
or the Black Order killed him during their
attack on the Asgardian ship.

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:07.020
And if the theories about Heimdall having
the Soul Stone are correct, then this could

00:04:07.020 --> 00:04:09.030
be how Thanos obtains that Stone.

00:04:09.030 --> 00:04:11.959
But I'm going to talk more about the Soul
Stone later.

00:04:11.959 --> 00:04:16.100
We do know that at least two characters survived
the attack on the Asgardian ship.

00:04:16.100 --> 00:04:21.139
Bruce Banner ends up back on Earth and although
Thor gets his head squeezed like a grape by

00:04:21.139 --> 00:04:25.110
Thanos, the God of Thunder survives this and
ends up with the Guardians.

00:04:25.110 --> 00:04:29.770
But Ryan asked what the chances are of Thor
making it out alive by the end of the movie.

00:04:29.770 --> 00:04:33.550
Well, my feeling right now is that it's about
50/50 for Thor.

00:04:33.550 --> 00:04:37.380
The Russos recently said that Thanos and Thor
were the two characters who would get the

00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:42.050
most screen time in Infinity War and we're
going to see Thor get some significant character

00:04:42.050 --> 00:04:43.400
development in the movie.

00:04:43.400 --> 00:04:48.180
As I mentioned in my last video, Thor's getting
a new hammer – and by the way, I think the

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:52.270
trailer's been digitally edited in this shot
to remove his new weapon so we can't see it

00:04:52.270 --> 00:04:53.270
yet.

00:04:53.270 --> 00:04:57.759
Thor's got his cape again here, plus there
are toys of Thor wielding his new weapon but

00:04:57.759 --> 00:05:01.710
without his eyepatch, just a scar around his
damaged eye.

00:05:01.710 --> 00:05:04.960
This all feels like Thor is going to be reborn
in a way.

00:05:04.960 --> 00:05:08.500
He's getting a new weapon and his full eyesight
will be restored.

00:05:08.500 --> 00:05:12.410
Now, all of these developments make me feel
it would be so cruel to watch the character

00:05:12.410 --> 00:05:15.860
go through this and then just be killed by
the end of Infinity War.

00:05:15.860 --> 00:05:20.330
So, I'm hoping Thor is one of the main Avengers
who survives through to Avengers 4.

00:05:20.330 --> 00:05:25.160
A very intriguing detail some of you noticed
was that when Cap goes up against Thanos,

00:05:25.160 --> 00:05:28.320
there's a little glint of yellow or perhaps
orange in his eyes.

00:05:28.320 --> 00:05:33.240
Now, that might just be the reflection from
the Infinity Gauntlet, however, there's speculation

00:05:33.240 --> 00:05:37.901
this might indicate that Cap is in possession
of or has the power of the Mind or the Soul

00:05:37.901 --> 00:05:38.901
Stone.

00:05:38.901 --> 00:05:43.770
It's possible that Steve Rogers has consumed
some of the Heart-Shaped Herb while in Wakanda.

00:05:43.770 --> 00:05:48.090
There's a theory that, ultimately, the herb
gains its powers from the Soul Stone, which

00:05:48.090 --> 00:05:52.699
was inside the meteorite that hit Wakanda,
meaning that the power of the Soul Stone could

00:05:52.699 --> 00:05:54.060
have transferred to Cap.

00:05:54.060 --> 00:05:58.220
And, yes, I know that Killmonger ordered the
destruction of the Heart-Shaped Herb in the

00:05:58.220 --> 00:06:03.319
Black Panther movie, however, it's possible
somebody saved some or that there's more elsewhere

00:06:03.319 --> 00:06:04.400
in the nation.

00:06:04.400 --> 00:06:08.199
These are interesting possibilities though
there's no concrete evidence I can see from

00:06:08.199 --> 00:06:13.210
the trailers so far, and it's quite possible
that the shot we see is simply Cap momentarily

00:06:13.210 --> 00:06:17.870
holding his own against Thanos, before the
Mad Titan crushes him, which sadly he did

00:06:17.870 --> 00:06:20.660
very easily in the Infinity Gauntlet comic.

00:06:20.660 --> 00:06:24.300
By the way, throughout the promos we've seen
so far we've only ever seen Thanos with a

00:06:24.300 --> 00:06:29.210
maximum of two Infinity Stones showing properly
in the gauntlet the power stone and the space

00:06:29.210 --> 00:06:30.210
stone.

00:06:30.210 --> 00:06:33.669
It's worth considering that Marvel might have
edited out other Infinity Stones from the

00:06:33.669 --> 00:06:38.280
trailers to prevent spoiling exactly how many
Thanos has at different points in the movie,

00:06:38.280 --> 00:06:42.240
in a similar way to how Thor's missing eye
in Ragnarok was restored in the trailers for

00:06:42.240 --> 00:06:43.240
that film.

00:06:43.240 --> 00:06:48.430
And talking of Infinity Stones, Roy Martin
Tandberg asks "What if the reason why Thanos

00:06:48.430 --> 00:06:53.830
wants to wipe out half the universe is to
get the Soul Stone, by capturing their souls?"

00:06:53.830 --> 00:06:58.030
Now, that's an interesting idea because so
far we've all mostly assumed that the Soul

00:06:58.030 --> 00:07:02.620
Stone exists in some kind of physical form,
but what if it's actually something more ethereal?

00:07:02.620 --> 00:07:07.280
I mean, in Thor: The Dark World when we were
introduced to the Aether, aka the Reality

00:07:07.280 --> 00:07:10.750
Stone, it was a liquid-like substance that
took over Jane Foster's body.

00:07:10.750 --> 00:07:16.330
"While the other relics often appear as stones,
the Aether is fluid and everchanging."

00:07:16.330 --> 00:07:18.879
"It changes matter into dark matter."

00:07:18.879 --> 00:07:24.460
"It seeks out host bodies, drawing strength
from their life-force."

00:07:24.460 --> 00:07:28.340
And in the comics, the Soul Gem is something
that draws in souls which would fit with the

00:07:28.340 --> 00:07:30.820
idea of Thanos capturing souls.

00:07:30.820 --> 00:07:35.930
The Soul Gem also has its own internal world
called Soulworld where the souls live that

00:07:35.930 --> 00:07:37.669
the gem has taken in.

00:07:37.669 --> 00:07:42.169
And because these are comic book movies, capturing
a character's soul would be a convenient way

00:07:42.169 --> 00:07:46.000
to appear to kill a character but have the
ability to bring them back when the remaining

00:07:46.000 --> 00:07:48.800
Avengers presumably defeat Thanos in Avengers
4.

00:07:48.800 --> 00:07:53.960
In fact, I actually think this might be what
happens to Gamora, Thanos's favourite daughter,

00:07:53.960 --> 00:07:57.199
and I talked about that in my recent Death
Theory video.

00:07:57.199 --> 00:08:00.090
But just where will the Soul Stone come into
play?

00:08:00.090 --> 00:08:04.389
Well, now that we have more details about
Thanos's homeworld Titan, I think there's

00:08:04.389 --> 00:08:09.270
a chance the Soul Stone location or discovery
will tie in with one of the action scenes

00:08:09.270 --> 00:08:12.259
on Titan or perhaps Thanos's backstory even.

00:08:12.259 --> 00:08:16.389
Other possibilities could be that the final
Infinity Stone is saved for a future movie

00:08:16.389 --> 00:08:20.270
like Captain Marvel or Ant-Man and the Wasp,
and I talked about those possibilities in

00:08:20.270 --> 00:08:22.569
my recent Soul Stone theory video.

00:08:22.569 --> 00:08:26.330
Some of you also want to know whether the
comic book character Death will be in Infinity

00:08:26.330 --> 00:08:29.979
War as she was an integral part of Thanos's
motivation in the comics.

00:08:29.979 --> 00:08:32.840
Well, I'm almost sure this won't be the case.

00:08:32.840 --> 00:08:36.250
Firstly, Marvel has gone with a different
motivation for Thanos which is related to

00:08:36.250 --> 00:08:39.060
the tragedy that happened to his homeworld
Titan.

00:08:39.060 --> 00:08:43.060
And secondly, I think Hela has potentially
taken the place of the Death character in

00:08:43.060 --> 00:08:44.500
the MCU.

00:08:44.500 --> 00:08:48.200
Hela is the Goddess of Death, after all, and
there's a possible hint that she knows or

00:08:48.200 --> 00:08:52.520
has a back story with Thanos as she knew that
Odin's Infinity Gauntlet was fake.

00:08:52.520 --> 00:08:57.490
In fact, I do think Hela could have survived
Ragnarok and might return in Infinity War

00:08:57.490 --> 00:09:01.560
perhaps either in a post-credits scene or
maybe in Avengers 4 where she could team up

00:09:01.560 --> 00:09:02.740
with Thanos.

00:09:02.740 --> 00:09:06.340
If you want to know more about Hela's possible
return, I'll link to a video I made about

00:09:06.340 --> 00:09:08.960
that in the description below.

00:09:08.960 --> 00:09:12.820
Another character who hasn't appeared in any
of the main trailers is Nebula.

00:09:12.820 --> 00:09:17.340
She did have a tiny appearance in the Super
Bowl TV spot, where she appeared looking angry

00:09:17.340 --> 00:09:20.020
and brandishing her electroshock weapon on
Titan.

00:09:20.020 --> 00:09:25.200
I'm hoping that as well as the film including
backstory for Gamora, we'll see more for Nebula

00:09:25.200 --> 00:09:26.200
too.

00:09:26.200 --> 00:09:29.730
As for what Nebula is up in the new movie,
in an interview, actress Karen Gillan has

00:09:29.730 --> 00:09:34.210
said that Nebula gets a new and unexpected
BFF in Infinity War.

00:09:34.210 --> 00:09:38.500
Gillan couldn't say who it was, but if it's
someone unexpected then I'm thinking she could

00:09:38.500 --> 00:09:43.260
be paired up with someone more humorous like
Spider-Man, perhaps even Ant-Man?

00:09:43.260 --> 00:09:47.800
Talking of Ant-Man, we haven't seen anything
at all of him or Hawkeye in the trailers or

00:09:47.800 --> 00:09:48.800
promo images.

00:09:48.800 --> 00:09:53.450
And I've got a separate video to explain where
they are plus who Game of Thrones star Peter

00:09:53.450 --> 00:09:55.880
Dinklage will be playing in Infinity War.

00:09:55.880 --> 00:09:58.690
I'll add a link here as soon as that video's
ready.

00:09:58.690 --> 00:10:03.430
OK, question for you guys now: Who do you
think will survive Infinity War and why?

00:10:03.430 --> 00:10:07.960
Let me know in the comments below, plus tell
me any requests for future Marvel videos.

